ASSEMBLY EXAMPLE - DIRECT SVC AND PC-RELATIVE DATA

Source adapted from userland/examples/asm/02-hello.s.
Write /tmp/ah.s via write_file:

  movs r0, #9
  movs r1, #1
  adr r2, msg
  movs r3, #6
  svc #0
  movs r0, #3
  movs r1, #0
  svc #0
  .align 2
  msg:
  .ascii "Hello\n"

Run separately:
  as /tmp/ah.s
  /tmp/a.out
Expected stdout: Hello and newline.

ABI: r0=9 write, r1=stdout fd, r2=buffer, r3=length.
Exit syscall r0=3, status in r1. These numbers are confirmed in
userland/examples/asm; for other numbers refer to the syscall header.
ADR needs forward aligned label within range (see /man/languages/asm).
Never hard-code relocated RAM pointers in a PIC program.
